# What do you think of online advertising?
I think online advertising has both advantages and disadvantages. On the positive side, it allows companies to reach a large number of people and target specific groups of customers. It can also be useful for consumers because we sometimes discover products or services that are actually relevant to us. However, too many online ads can be annoying and intrusive, especially when they interrupt what we're watching or reading. I'm also concerned about privacy because many companies collect our personal data to show us targeted advertisements. So overall, I think online advertising can be useful, but there needs to be a balance between effective advertising and respecting people's privacy.

# Are there any greate online advertisements?
Yes, definitely. I think there are quite a few great online advertisements, especially the ones that tell a good story rather than simply trying to sell a product. For example, I’ve seen some ads on YouTube that show how a product can make people’s daily lives easier, and they often use humor or emotional stories to catch viewers’ attention. What I like about these advertisements is that they don’t feel like traditional commercials. They’re entertaining and memorable, so people are more likely to remember the brand or product afterward. I think the best online ads are the ones that can entertain people while still getting their message across.

# What do people usually buy?
I think people usually buy things that they need in their everyday lives, such as food, clothes, household items, and personal care products. Nowadays, people also spend quite a lot of money on electronics, especially smartphones, laptops, and other gadgets. Apart from basic necessities, many people spend money on things like entertainment, eating out, and traveling. Of course, what people buy depends a lot on their income and lifestyle. For example, people with higher incomes may be more willing to spend money on expensive brands or luxury products, while others tend to focus more on essential items.

# Why does buying new things make people happy?
I think buying new things can make people happy for a few reasons. First of all, there's a sense of excitement that comes from getting something new, especially if it's something we've wanted for a long time. New products can also make our lives more comfortable or convenient, which can give us a feeling of satisfaction. For example, buying a new phone might make someone happy because it has better features and makes certain tasks easier. However, I think this kind of happiness is often temporary because people usually get used to their new possessions after a while. So, the excitement may gradually disappear.

# Do people watch useless advertising in this day and age?
Yes, definitely. I think people still come across a lot of useless or irrelevant advertisements these days, especially online. For example, when we're watching videos or browsing social media, we often see ads for products or services that we're not interested in. Most of the time, people simply skip them or scroll past them without paying much attention. However, some ads can still catch our attention if they're funny, creative, or relevant to our interests. So, I think people do see a lot of useless advertising, but they don't necessarily pay attention to it.
